# BAIME experiment throwaway checkouts / build output — never track
**/worktrees/
# gap-gitignore-worktree-scratch-dirs-kills-round4-false-red (2026-08-07): worktree-scratch
# coordination dirs left at the repo root by the --loop quay-init worktree-root tests
# (.quay-worktree-local/, .quay-worktree-local2/, .quay-wtl3/). Same gitignored family as
# worktrees/ — untracked scratch, NOT test products; if left un-ignored they trip the suite-after
# dirty-tree assertion (round-4 false red). First line of defense (git status never shows them);
# complement to the assert-clean-tree exclusion, cross-annotated with
# gap-assert-clean-tree-premise-void-under-concurrent-writers (AC3).
# No trailing slash: `git check-ignore` must match these names even when absent
# (the Contract measure counts 3 matches), not only when the scratch dirs exist.
**/.quay-worktree-local*
**/.quay-wtl*
**/dist-sea/
**/dist-sea-release/
**/.quay/gate-events.jsonl
**/.quay/supervisor-bus-ledger.jsonl
# gap-assert-clean-tree-premise-void-under-concurrent-writers (2026-08-07): the before-run
# porcelain snapshots for the suite-AFTER DELTA assertions (assert-clean-tree.sh --snapshot /
# tmux-leak-scan.sh --snapshot). Same gitignored runtime-state family as gate-events.jsonl — a
# snapshot is per-run transient state that must never appear in `git status --porcelain` (if it
# did, the suite-AFTER check would see its own snapshot as NEW dirt).
**/.quay/assert-clean-tree.snapshot
**/.quay/tmux-leak-scan.snapshot
